\begin{abstract}
We present the SupraKernel Sovereign Autonomous Intelligence Loop, a
four-stage autodidact architecture designed for autonomous inference,
policy generation, patch execution, and cryptographic verification.
The system integrates ring-zero privilege separation, tensor-parallel
telemetry ingestion, Lyapunov-based stability control, and Merkle-anchored
auditability. We provide formal mathematical proofs of stability,
quantitative stress-test results across extreme compute regimes, and
a rigorous description of the autonomous recovery loop.
\end{abstract}

\section{Introduction}
The SupraKernel architecture is a sovereign autonomous intelligence loop
capable of continuous self-correction, policy refinement, and tamper-evident
execution. The system is composed of four phases:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item Telemetry ingestion.
    \item Reflection and causal inference.
    \item Autonomous policy generation.
    \item Patch execution and Merkle verification.
\end{enumerate}
A ring-zero execution core ensures privileged control-plane isolation,
while Lyapunov stability guarantees bounded autonomous behavior.

