\section{Autonomous Recovery Loop}
When instability is detected, the kernel executes:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item Drift interception via Lyapunov thresholding.
    \item State rollback to last verified Merkle epoch.
    \item Dynamic scaling of damping matrix $Q$.
\end{enumerate}
This ensures safe return to the stable basin of attraction.

\section{Cryptographic Auditability}
Each epoch is hashed into a Merkle tree:
\[
h_{\text{epoch}} = H(\Theta, \text{policy}, \text{patch}),
\]
ensuring tamper-evident, append-only logging.

